# Reference data and settings (AdminService, /service/admin)
#
# Tags and response templates are read by everyone, created by agents and changed or deleted by their
# creator or by an administrator. The settings are changed by administrators only. Start the app
# with `npm run cds-watch` (http://localhost:4004) and run the requests top down. The users are
# the mocked users (the password is the user name).

@host = http://localhost:4004

### Tags
# expect: 200
GET {{host}}/service/admin/Tags?$orderby=code&$select=code,title
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### Search the tags
# expect: 200
GET {{host}}/service/admin/Tags?$search=delivery&$select=code,title
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### A viewer may not create a tag
# expect: 403
POST {{host}}/service/admin/Tags
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "recall",
  "title": "Product recall"
}

### An agent creates a tag
# expect: 201
POST {{host}}/service/admin/Tags
Authorization: Basic agent agent
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "recall",
  "title": "Product recall"
}

### The code must be a slug (lower case words separated by hyphens)
# expect: 400
POST {{host}}/service/admin/Tags
Authorization: Basic agent agent
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "Not A Slug",
  "title": "Invalid"
}

### The creator changes the tag
# expect: 200
PATCH {{host}}/service/admin/Tags('recall')
Authorization: Basic agent agent
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Product recall (safety)"
}

### The change history of the tag
# expect: 200
GET {{host}}/service/admin/Tags('recall')/changes?$select=attribute,valueChangedFrom,valueChangedTo,createdBy&$orderby=createdAt
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### Delete the tag
# expect: 204
DELETE {{host}}/service/admin/Tags('recall')
Authorization: Basic agent agent

### Response templates that are valid now
# expect: 200
GET {{host}}/service/admin/ResponseTemplates?$orderby=code&$select=code,title,messageCategory,validFrom,validTo
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### The templates as they were valid on 1 March 2025 (time travel with sap-valid-at)
# expect: 200
GET {{host}}/service/admin/ResponseTemplates?$orderby=code&$select=code,title,validFrom,validTo&sap-valid-at=2025-03-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### All versions of one template (sap-valid-from and sap-valid-to select a period)
# expect: 200
GET {{host}}/service/admin/ResponseTemplates?$filter=code%20eq%20'warranty-claim'&$orderby=validFrom&sap-valid-from=2024-01-01T00:00:00Z&sap-valid-to=2026-01-01T00:00:00Z
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### The application settings
# expect: 200
GET {{host}}/service/admin/Settings
Authorization: Basic viewer viewer

### An agent may not change the settings
# expect: 403
PATCH {{host}}/service/admin/Settings
Authorization: Basic agent agent
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "autoEnrichment": false
}

### An administrator switches the AI enrichment off
# expect: 200
PATCH {{host}}/service/admin/Settings
Authorization: Basic admin admin
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "autoEnrichment": false
}

### ...and selects the model for the next time
# expect: 200
PATCH {{host}}/service/admin/Settings
Authorization: Basic admin admin
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "autoEnrichment": true,
  "aiModelName": "gpt-4.1-mini"
}
